# The M8 Hyper-V check's release run (tools/hyperv/README.md, "At the M8
# check"; docs/design.md, "The Hyper-V check"): tests/qemu/release.scenario's
# steps with what differs on Hyper-V, for M7's 16550 questions. The release
# kernel prints nothing; everything after the loader comes from uart. Root
# issues no exit port, since this is not QEMU, and halts after TEST PASS;
# the script turns the VM off. The line typed is 14 bytes, whose last 6
# stay below the receive FIFO's trigger of 8, so only the character
# timeout delivers them: the line must still be read whole. uart's burst
# is 15 with working FIFOs or 1 without (both start "burst 1"), and its
# THRE bursts must be above 0. Run it again with -ConnectAfterSeconds 20:
# the script then types the line when "release: type a line" arrives, or
# after 10 s with no line, and reports how many of uart's lines above the
# send:, from "root: cmdline" on, arrived (all: the transmitter waits for
# a client; none: it drains); the steps after the send: must pass either
# way.
cmdline: test=release
kernel: release
exit: success
expect: loader: microL4 loader
expect: entering kernel
next: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=release"
expect: root: image frames: slots
expect: root: empty: slots
expect: release: watch (priority 255), uart (priority 200) with the COM1 IOPort and IRQ 4, console (priority 150); exit port none: not QEMU
expect: release: a probe thread's DebugPutChar, DebugHalt, DebugDumpScheduler and reserved numbers 19 and 31 each raised UnknownSyscall with the number in MR18
expect: release: type a line
send: release input\r
expect: release: read "release input"
expect: release: uart:
expect: , 14 bytes received,
expect: , 0 overruns, 0 line errors,
expect: , burst 1                  # 15 with working FIFOs, 1 without
expect: TEST PASS
forbid: microL4 kernel
forbid: bootinfo:
forbid: DEBUG HALT
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
forbid: , 0 THRE bursts
